From 34ee63e6bfcbf755d69b6596ff13584df848c268 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:38:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MOTORVIEW-LED (web): Motor View -- the 11 lamps are golden's
 (Ready = MotorHomeLed green from HomeFlag; the other 10 = MOT[].Led[] red
 from the runtime led{}), unknown values hatched, and number columns show
 "---" instead of a fake 0

Teach / motor pages audit: Ready was "not alarm" (red on every healthy axis), Home was HomeFlag, CW/CCW were the speed
sign, EMG / soft limits hard-coded false, S Alarm copied Alarm; Target / Can / L / M / R always 0. Now
[homeDone, led.cw, led.home, led.ccw, led.emg, led.alarm, led.softCw, led.softCcw, led.sAlarm, led.inPos, led.servoOn]
(golden SetMotorMonitor main.cpp:22495-22524, MotorHomeLed :14321-14326); Target = position.targetPos; Can/L/M/R "---"
(no such fields in the runtime JSON -- nothing invented); Speed = cur.readSpeed (golden GetSpeed). Headless with a
48-row fixture: 343/343 checks (the old page 26/343).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 page/Main.MotorView.html | 110 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 80 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

